<article>
<nav class="mb-24" aria-label="UI navigation"><a href="/ui/">UI library</a> / <a href="/ui/cards/" aria-current="page">Cards</a></nav>
<h1 class="fs-37 lh-37 mb-24">Cards</h1>
<p class="mb-32">The vertical card and two horizontal variants share the same image, heading, topic labels, and short lesson on spacing.</p>
<nav class="flex flex-wrap gap-16 mb-24" aria-label="Card examples"><a href="#author-profile">Author profile</a></nav>
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Vertical card</h2>
<p class="mb-24">The card keeps its original <code>max-width: 344px</code> and shrinks with the available space. Both the card and its image use <code>border-r-16</code>.</p>
{% set markup %}{% include "components/cards/vertical.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(markup, "Vertical blog card") }}
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Horizontal card, image left</h2>
<p class="mb-24">Both horizontal variants give the image link wrapper <code>mb-24 mb-lg-0</code>: a 1.5rem bottom margin while stacked, reset to zero from 960 pixels when the horizontal gap takes over.</p>
<p class="mb-24"><code>flex-lg</code> places the image and content side by side from 960 pixels, with equal <code>flex-1</code> halves and <code>gap-24</code> between them. Below large, the image stacks above the text.</p>
{% set horizontal %}{% include "components/cards/horizontal.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(horizontal, "Horizontal blog card") }}
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Horizontal card, image right</h2>
<p class="mb-24">Put the image first in the HTML so it stacks above the text on smaller screens. Add <code>order-lg-last</code> to the image link wrapper: from 960 pixels, <code>order: 1</code> moves it after the content, placing the image on the right when <code>flex-lg</code> makes the card horizontal.</p>
{% set horizontalRight %}{% include "components/cards/horizontal-right.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(horizontalRight, "Horizontal image-right card") }}
<h2 id="author-profile" class="fs-24 lh-32 mb-16">Author profile for a sidebar</h2>
<p class="mb-24">An unboxed profile capped at 344px, also usable in a 268px sidebar. The portrait sits beside a vertically centered name, role and social row; the biography spans the width below. Flex wrapping moves the text below the portrait when space becomes tight. The few inline dimensions keep the copied example self-contained without adding library utilities.</p>
{% set author %}{% include "components/cards/author.njk" %}{% endset %}
{{ example(author, "Sidebar author profile", "", false, "author-profile-code", authorExample.copyNotice) }}
<p>Alex Example is a demo author. Links point to example.com; replace them with your own profile and feed URLs. Replace the neutral avatar with an image you can use. Its empty alt avoids repeating the adjacent name; write meaningful alt text if your replacement conveys additional information.</p>
<p>Social marks use inherited text color and labeled links. The displayed code omits license comments for readability; <strong>Copy HTML includes one consolidated Bootstrap Icons MIT notice</strong> for the complete card. Keep that notice when reusing it. Read the <a href="/assets/licenses/bootstrap-icons-LICENSE.txt">full notice</a> or browse <a href="/ui/icons/#icons-social-and-feeds">individual social/feed SVGs and brand guidance</a>. Standalone Copy SVG includes each icon's notice.</p>
